-- Task review follow-up (Important 2): the seeded "warning" status
-- color shipped in 0032_site_branding.sql (#B45309, Tailwind amber-700)
-- only reaches 4.18:1 contrast against the seeded light surface
-- (osi-cream-100 / #F2E9DE) -- below the 4.5:1 WCAG AA normal-text
-- threshold. lib/branding/schema.ts's brandingConfigV1Schema now
-- contrast-checks the four status roles (error/success/warning/info)
-- against lightSurface the same way it already checked textOnLight/
-- mutedTextOnLight (previously it validated only that the four status
-- roles resolved to a real swatch, never their actual contrast) -- which
-- means the ORIGINAL 0032 seed no longer parses against the corrected
-- schema. This migration corrects the two singleton rows in place to
-- osi-status-warning = #92400E (5.90:1 on osi-cream-100, 6.83:1 on the
-- "technical plate" raised surface #FFFAF4 -- both comfortably above
-- 4.5:1) -- see docs/DECISIONS.md for the full rationale and numbers.
--
-- No schema/table/RLS/function change here, only a data correction --
-- draft_version/published_version are deliberately left unchanged
-- (still 1): no admin session has ever read/cached an expected_version
-- for this singleton row yet (no admin UI exists in this phase), so
-- there's nothing to invalidate by editing the row's content directly,
-- unlike a real edit through save_branding_draft_atomic.
--
-- Generated via `pnpm exec tsx scripts/print-branding-seed.ts` against
-- the corrected lib/branding/seed.ts, not hand-typed, for the same
-- anti-drift reason 0032's original seed literal was.

update site_branding
